      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Many Echeveria hybrids are sold; this row is the species. Watering: NC State says overwatering is the most common problem and it likes dry, well-drained soil; RHS says water moderately in growth and not at all when dormant; both fit let_fully_dry but neither says 'fully' (agent mapping). Light: both full sun. Size: RHS up to 10 cm tall, spread 10 to 50 cm (upper stored); NC State gives no height. Hardiness: RHS H2 (1 to 5 C) and NC State zones 9a to 11b, no indoor range. Toxicity: only NC State's tags (non-toxic for cats and dogs) say anything; the ASPCA echeveria page returned 404 and RHS is silent. One tag-only source: review. Growth: NC State slow."
      },
